Specifically:

  spec/openapi.json is a verbatim vendored copy of that project's OpenAPI
  document. spec/README.md records the upstream commit it came from.

  internal/api/api.gen.go is generated from that document by oapi-codegen. Its
  Go types mirror the document's schemas, and its doc comments reproduce the
  document's own schema and property descriptions.

  event.go and enums.go declare Go types and constants mirroring those schemas,
  and their doc comments reproduce the document's descriptions.

How these files are produced has changed more than once, and it does not change
what they derive from. The descriptions are the upstream project's whether a
generator copied them or a person did, so this attribution applies either way.
A test keeps the list above exhaustive in both directions, over the root package
and internal/api: see TestNoticeNamesEveryFileCarryingUpstreamProse.

Attribution notices in the upstream project's NOTICE file that pertain to its
Python runtime dependencies are omitted here, as this Software contains no part
of them — Apache License 2.0 section 4(d) provides for excluding notices that do
not pertain to any part of a Derivative Work.
